[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106258,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Solitary circumscribed neuroma (SCN) is a benign, often cutaneous, nodular proliferation of nerve fibres with Schwann cells predominating over axons, showing a strong predilection for the face.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106259,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9570/0 Solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n<p>9570/0 Plexiform solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106260,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F24 &amp; XH90Y8 Benign cutaneous neoplasms of neural or nerve sheath origin &amp; Solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106261,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> palisaded encapsulated neuroma; palisaded and encapsulated neuroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106262,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plexiform solitary circumscribed neuroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106263,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The skin of the face (particularly the nose, forehead, and lips) hosts approximately 90% of SCNs. Many lesions occur in proximity to mucocutaneous junctions or even affect oral mucosa; the latter represents the most common non-cutaneous site {20237984}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106264,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with SCN usually present with a slow-growing, firm, painless, circumscribed dermal-based nodule. SCN is mostly solitary, but rare examples of multiple SCNs have been reported, with no evidence of any associated systemic disease {26460241}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106265,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN is most common in the fifth to seventh decades of life, but it can occur in patients of any age. There is no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106266,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106267,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN is a benign tumour of nerve fibres, with slow growth over many years; it is unrelated to trauma {2660609}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106268,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN usually appears as a flesh-coloured papule &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;mm in diameter. It is a circumscribed dermal-based nodule with a firm, pale-grey cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106269,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN is a circumscribed dermal-based tumour composed of bland spindle-shaped cells with wavy nuclei in a background of hyalinized collagen. The cells often form well-developed fascicles, and some palisading of nuclei within the tumour is characteristically present. A thin perineurial-derived fibrous capsule may surround the lesion, but it is often incomplete at the superficial aspect. Artefactual clefting is a frequent finding, and extension into the subcutis may be present on occasion {4639250}. No cytological atypia is present and mitoses are inconspicuous. Occasional cases showed degenerative nuclear changes or focal epithelioid cytology. The overlying epidermis is usually normal or attenuated. The spindle cells are strongly and diffusely positive for S100. NFP staining typically identifies the presence of small nerve fibres within the tumour {1705947}. Perineurial cells in the capsule stain for EMA, claudin-1, and GLUT1 {20237984}. Occasionally, SCNs may have a multinodular or plexiform growth pattern {19614730}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106270,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FNAB of SCN shows a nonspecific paucicellular pattern of bland spindle cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106271,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No diagnostic molecular findings have been described.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106272,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a circumscribed cutaneous lesion of Schwann cell&ndash;rich fascicles of nerve fibres with or without partial encapsulation; focal palisading and artefactual clefting; S100 positivity with focal NFP staining; the peripheral capsule is highlighted by perineurial markers (EMA, GLUT1).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106273,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106274,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 189,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SCN is a benign tumour with no capacity for metastasis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T14:06:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]